# SteamVault Android app -- release signing config (WP 4b.9).
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` (same directory, i.e. `app/`,
# next to this example) and fill in the real values. `keystore.properties`
# is gitignored (see app/.gitignore -- reserved for exactly this since
# WP 4b.1) and must NEVER be committed: it is one properties file away from
# leaking the signing key that lets an attacker publish updates to your own
# users under your app's identity.
#
# You create the keystore yourself -- see app/README.md's "Release build,
# signing, and distribution" section for the exact `keytool` command, what
# to answer at each prompt, and how to verify the resulting APK afterwards.
#
# `storeFile` may be an absolute path, or a path relative to this `app/`
# directory (Gradle's `file(...)` resolves relative paths against the
# project directory that declares them, i.e. `app/app/`'s parent -- see
# app/app/build.gradle.kts's signing section). Keeping the real keystore
# OUTSIDE this repo entirely (e.g. in your home directory) is the safer
# default; a path inside `app/` would also work since *.jks/*.keystore are
# gitignored too, but outside is one less thing to double-check.
#
# On Windows, use a real Windows path (`C:/Users/you/...` or
# `C:\\Users\\you\\...`), not a Git-Bash-style `/c/Users/...` path --
# Gradle's `file(...)` does not understand that mount-point syntax and will
# treat it as a RELATIVE path, silently joining it onto the module
# directory instead of the drive root. This fails loudly (a "keystore file
# not found" error naming the wrong, joined-together path), so it is not a
# security or correctness risk -- just a confusing first error worth
# knowing about in advance.
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/your/steamvault-release.jks
storePassword=change-me
keyAlias=steamvault
keyPassword=change-me

# Equivalent environment-variable fallback (CI-style; no properties file
# needed): VAULT_RELEASE_STORE_FILE, VAULT_RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD,
# VAULT_RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS, VAULT_RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD. This properties file
# takes precedence over the environment when both are present -- see
# app/app/build.gradle.kts's `releaseSigningValue` helper.
